Apple macOS SDK linker interfaces

These unmodified text-based linker interface files originate in Apple's macOS
26.2 SDK (build 25C58), supplied with Xcode 26.3 (build 17C529). The accompanying
Xcode-and-Apple-SDKs-Agreement.rtf is the original agreement from that Xcode
distribution. Apple retains any applicable rights. These files and that
agreement are not covered by Roc Signals' Universal Permissive License (UPL),
Version 1.0.

The files contain interface metadata, not Apple's framework implementations.
Roc performs the final application link on the user's machine when the user
builds an application, including the build step of `roc build`. These .tbd files
are linking stubs used in that step. Running an already-built executable does
not perform that build-time link again; macOS loads the required system
libraries and frameworks at runtime.

Applications require the framework implementations supplied by macOS on
Apple-branded hardware. The bundled stubs currently allow the final application
link without a separately installed Apple SDK or Xcode. An Apple SDK is used
to build the platform's native host and obtain these interface files; it is
not a runtime implementation and is not currently required from end users.

